{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7afd1d2b0c207cdeb761bebd4d0ac5605bc3d30b35aeb8a2dabdcf140ab93190","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review gate - LLM model routing and step execution","key_entities":["code-review.yaml","PydanticAIRunner.run","resolve_model","usage_log.record","RunRequest","runner.py:547","ContextVar","gate_dispatch.py","_effective_config","model_classes.py","CODE_NAMES"],"problem_keywords":["per-step model class","code-review gate","model resolution","wiring","runner configuration","declaration ignored"],"propositions":["Per-step model class declarations in code-review.yaml are silently ignored at runtime; every step executes with cfg.model instead of its declared class","PydanticAIRunner.run discards req.config.model and uses only the model baked into self._config at runner construction time","Step 0 adds ContextVar-based observability to record step ID and declared model class token in usage logs, enabling per-step attribution","The fix (one line: cfg = _effective_config(self._config, req)) substitutes req.config.model into a copy of the runner's config before resolution, making per-step declarations effective across code-review and plan-review gates"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787484763753757001,"uuid":"469e9402-3fa1-41a3-9d2f-c4e9e656a8ab"}